# CFF 1.2.0 is the latest released schema. 1.3.0 is unreleased: no validator
# accepts it (cffconvert: 'Unrecognized value for key "cff-version"') and GitHub's
# "Cite this repository" widget breaks on it. citation-version.yml validates this
# file on every release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "GBIF Gap Finder: a reproducible pipeline for biodiversity data gap analysis"
abstract: >-
  An R/targets and Shiny pipeline that quantifies spatial, temporal, and
  taxonomic gaps in a country's GBIF-mediated occurrence data. It combines
  GBIF occurrence cubes with a national taxonomic backbone and national
  red list, invasive (GRIIS), and sensitive species lists, resolving all
  source citations and DOIs automatically from their download and dataset
  keys.
type: software
